%I A397012 #46 Sep 01 2026 19:39:00
%S A397012 0,1,3,4,7,9,10,12,13,16,18,19,22,25,27,28,30,31,34,36,39,43,45,46,49,
%T A397012 52,54,55,58,61,63,64,66,67,70,72,73,79,81,82,84,85,88,90,93,94,99,
%U A397012 100,103,108,109,111,112,117,118,120,121,124,126,127,130,133
%N A397012 Numbers that are a sum of three triangular numbers whose indices are in arithmetic progression; i.e., numbers of the form 3*T(k) + d^2, where T(k) = k*(k+1)/2 and k, d are integers.
%C A397012 m is a term if and only if the exponent of p in 8*m+3 is even for every prime p == 13, 17, 19, 23 (mod 24).
%C A397012 No term is congruent to 2 (mod 3).
%C A397012 The number of terms not exceeding X is asymptotic to 2*kappa*X/sqrt(log X), where kappa = (1/2)*(3/2)^(1/4)*Product_{p == 13, 17, 19, 23 (mod 24)} (1 - p^(-2))^(-1/2) = 0.5583571... . The constant is exactly twice the corresponding constant for A002480, a Landau-type constant for the non-principal class of discriminant -24.
%o A397012 (PARI) isok(n) = my(f=factor(8*n+3)); for(i=1, #f~, if(setsearch([13,17,19,23], f[i,1]%24) && f[i,2]%2, return(0))); 1
%Y A397012 Cf. A002480 (the corresponding set for three squares in arithmetic progression; n is a term iff 8*n+3 is in A002480), A084865 (primes in A002480), A000217 (triangular numbers), A000075.
%K A397012 nonn,easy,new
%O A397012 1,3
%A A397012 _Mohammad F. Marashdeh_, Aug 26 2026
